@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Deploy Commands
  "CLI handlers for mason deploy and mason status with plan, progress, and summary output."

  Provides:
    - cli.newDeployCommand @source("symbol:newDeployCommand")
    - cli.newStatusCommand @source("symbol:newStatusCommand")
    - cli.defaultDeployRun @source("symbol:defaultDeployRun")

  Consumes:
    - config.Config.Site
    - deploy.Service
    - output.WriteJSON
    - remote.SSHOptionsFromServer

  Invariants:
    - The optional [site] argument MUST select a site by name or host; none selects the project's default site
    - status MUST always run as a dry-run plan and MUST NOT transfer bytes; deploy --dry-run MUST behave the same
    - deploy MUST require confirmation before --delete removes remote files unless --yes
    - The build folder MUST resolve relative to the project file's directory, not the working directory
    - Before planning, deploy MUST verify the site's path exists and is writable, failing with 'mason provision' as the fix
    - build: . MUST warn on stderr only when the project looks like source (node_modules/ or package.json); a plain HTML project MUST deploy without noise
    - On a terminal, transfer progress MUST render as one in-place line; with -v as raw rsync lines; otherwise a single 'Sending …' line
    - Plain output MUST show the site, build folder, plan line, and summary or up-to-date message

  OutOfScope:
    - Deploy planner parsing (owned by internal/deploy)
    - mason init scaffolding (future M-062)

  Scenario (happy-path): Status plan
    Given a successful deploy plan
    When status runs
    Then plan output is rendered without deploying

  Scenario (happy-path): Deploy with changes
    Given a plan with files to send and confirmation skipped via --yes
    When deploy runs
    Then plan and summary output are rendered

  Scenario (negative): Delete confirmation declined
    Given --delete with files to remove and no --yes
    When the user declines confirmation
    Then deploy exits without transferring bytes
